<title>GERMANY: Hong Kong's Yam happy to continue after handover.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong's Yam happy to continue after handover.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Joseph Yam, chief executive of the Hong Kong monetary authority, said on Thursday that he was happy to continue in his position after the handover of the colony to China on June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm happy to continue in my position. No one has asked me to step down and I need a job,&quot; Yam told journalists after a conference in Frankfurt on Hong Kong's monetary arrangements through 1997.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
